er  seven a true hero will fall at some  point in their Journey long before Gal  Gadot achieved stardom for the role of  Wonder Woman she was working a lot as an  actress and model in Tel Aviv she would  audition for so many projects in  Hollywood but she never broke through  this profession the rejection dude it's  a toughness it wasn't until she  auditioned for Wonder Woman and pushed  so hard to get the role that she finally  made her Mark she inspirationally said  it's also proof that everything happens  for a reason I was on the verge of  giving up acting and then this happened  number eight you can still quit while  you're on top and all it takes is one  project Jennifer Aniston had  contemplated quitting the business after  a rough experience during during filming  an unnamed project this experience was  so rough for her that she thought about  quitting I would have to say the last  two years that quitting has crossed my  mind which it never did before the  project had sucked the life out of me I  don't know if this is what interests me  number nine the worst of tragedies can  sometimes cause us to fall back into  normal life Mark Ruffalo had achieved  success in the early 2000s but after the  passing of his brother he decided to  pack up his family and leave Hollywood  he just never thought he would get back  into it being that his brother was  highly regarded in that Community number  10 being a child in Showbiz is tougher  than you think for Brie Larson she  auditioned so much as a child and teen  but never got a role she took rejection  so personally and even ran away from  home a few times I ran around the block  and then came back after taking multiple  breaks and focusing on other Ventures  she was able to find true love with the  craft itself rather than just focusing  on getting the role this is what feels  like my purpose it feels like what I'm  here to do number 11 Daniel caluya just  really wanted to get out before getting  his star role after his breakout role on  black mirror in the episode 15 million  merits he was surprisingly not booking  any jobs when it came time to audition  for get out Daniel was not in a good  space with acting I was really  disillusioned with acting I had stopped  acting for like a year and a half I  checked out because I was just like this  isn't working when he booked that  life-changing role it changed his  mindset completely Jordan Peele quite  literally saved his career number 12  Henry Cavill auditioned for Twilight  we're not saying that he wouldn't have  been perfect or anything but his  audition for Edward was actually far  from perfect it was so horrible in fact  that he was about ready to throw in the  cape the audition was one of the worst  auditions I did in my whole life I  remember calling my parents and saying  I'm done I can't torture myself anymore  number 13 inspiration can come from  anyone not just the old wise folks  Michael B Jordan did a lot to get his  role in Fruitvale Station he went to  hundreds of auditions and got constant  rejections causing him to think about  quitting more than a few times by the  time filming had begun Michael was tired  of the business but all it took was an  inspiration like director Ryan coogler  to keep him grounded he's the reason why  I have the self-confidence to go out  there and do it behind the camera to see  somebody my age taking care of however  many hundreds of millions of dollars  this movie is it's inspiring it lets me  know that I can do that as well number  14 you do too much in a short amount of  time and it'll burn you out real quick  this was the case for Channing Tatum who  had done a whopping 20 films in a span  of six years he thought he'd done enough  and maybe it was time to retire from the  industry he said I took four movies back  back to back without any time off and I  wasn't as good as I wanted to be in  those last two movies because I didn't  have the energy I asked myself do I want  to act anymore 